course: dictionary
lesson: 5732
title: Lose and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. Lose is a good example. «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» Here lose does not mean dropping something. It means you no longer know where you are in the text.
explain: Lose is a verb that changes its form: lose, loses, lost, losing. «Because energy is lost at each step, there are always far fewer predators than plant-eaters.» Lost tells you something has gone away, so less energy is left at each step.
explain: When you meet lose, ask what is gone, what is not won, or what you now have less of. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: To lose something is to no longer have it, often by mistake, as in lose a glove.
fact: To lose a game is to not win it.
fact: To lose your way is to not know where you are.
fact: To lose weight, time or money is to have less of it.
fact: If you get lost, stay where you are and find a safe adult.
exercise: «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» What does lose your place mean? | You have run away from school | *You no longer know where you are in the text | You have won the race | You have dropped your pencil case
exercise: Mia says, «I can't find my glove, I must have lost it.» What does lost mean here? | It was found under the bed | *No longer had it, often by mistake | It was won in a game | It had less time left
exercise: «Losing or changing one small word can change a whole meaning.» What does losing mean in this sentence? | Making a word bigger | Winning a word game | *Not having a word any more, so the meaning changes | Writing a word twice
test: Sam's team lost the match. What does lost a game mean? | To win it easily | To play it at home | To watch it from the side | *To not win it
test: «If you get lost, stay where you are and find a safe adult.» What should you do if you get lost? | *Stay where you are and find a safe adult | Hide behind a tree | Run as fast as you can to find home | Keep walking until you see someone
exam: Ben had 9 pencils and lost 5. How many pencils does he have now? | *4 | 5 | 14 | 3
